      "figure": {
        "svgShape": "productivity-figure",
        "parametricParams": {
          "family": "threshold",
          "divisions": 5,
          "mark": 5
        }
      },
      "procedureFull": "1. At the close of a work session, intentionally leave the final task slightly unfinished with an obvious, low-effort next step (e.g., write a failing test with a simple syntax fix).\n2. Document the next action in a single comment right at the top of the working file.\n3. When sitting down the next day, begin by executing that simple, pre-planned step.\n4. Use the quick completion of this initial micro-task to generate the momentum needed for deeper work.",
      "setupFull": "`# ON-RAMP FOR TOMORROW MORNING:`\n``# The test below fails because `response.status_code` returns 403 instead of 200.``\n``# Fix: Add `auth_token` header to test client fixture in line 42.``\n`def test_endpoint_returns_ok():`\n    `response = client.get(\"/api/v1/health\")`\n    `assert response.status_code == 200`",
      "trapFull": "Cleaning up, polishing, and checking in all work at the end of the day, forcing a cold start from a completely blank state the following morning.",
